  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find positions of 2 and 3\n    pos2 = None\n    pos3 = None\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2:\n                pos2 = (r, c)\n            elif grid[r][c] == 3:\n                pos3 = (r, c)\n    \n    # Create a copy of the grid\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # If either 2 or 3 is missing, return the copy unchanged\n    if pos2 is None or pos3 is None:\n        return result\n    \n    r2, c2 = pos2\n    r3, c3 = pos3\n    \n    # Draw horizontal line from 2 towards 3's column (excluding positions of 2 and 3)\n    if c2 < c3:\n        for c in range(c2 + 1, c3):\n            result[r2][c] = 8\n    elif c2 > c3:\n        for c in range(c3 + 1, c2):\n            result[r2][c] = 8\n    \n    # Draw vertical line from the intersection towards 3 (excluding positions of 2 and 3)\n    if r2 < r3:\n        for r in range(r2 + 1, r3):\n            result[r][c3] = 8\n    elif r2 > r3:\n        for r in range(r3 + 1, r2):\n            result[r][c3] = 8\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find positions of 2 and 3\n    pos2 = None\n    pos3 = None\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2:\n                pos2 = (r, c)\n            elif grid[r][c] == 3:\n                pos3 = (r, c)\n    \n    # Create a copy of the grid\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # If either 2 or 3 is missing, return the copy unchanged\n    if pos2 is None or pos3 is None:\n        return result\n    \n    r2, c2 = pos2\n    r3, c3 = pos3\n    \n    # Draw horizontal line from 2 towards 3's column (excluding positions of 2 and 3)\n    if c2 < c3:\n        for c in range(c2 + 1, c3):\n            result[r2][c] = 8\n    elif c2 > c3:\n        for c in range(c3 + 1, c2):\n            result[r2][c] = 8\n    \n    # Draw vertical line from the intersection towards 3 (excluding positions of 2 and 3)\n    if r2 < r3:\n        for r in range(r2 + 1, r3):\n            result[r][c3] = 8\n    elif r2 > r3:\n        for r in range(r3 + 1, r2):\n            result[r][c3] = 8\n    \n    return result",
